Description: Dialogs that belong to no window yet sit on their app's taskbar pin, and Open and Save dialogs attach to their window
 Document Recovery, and the dialog that saves documents when LibreOffice
 crashes, come up before any document window, so they kept LibreOffice's
 own icon and, on Wayland, the libreoffice-startcenter app_id: a plain
 taskbar button of their own. They now take the icon of the app whose
 documents they save or recover (Writer's when none is known), which with
 wildos-window-app-id.patch also gives them that app's app_id.
 .
 The Qt file picker asked the desktop portal for its Open and Save dialog
 with no parent window, so the dialog had a taskbar button of its own and
 the document stayed usable behind it. It now names the window the way
 Qt's own portal dialogs do, through Qt's private platform services: on
 Wayland an xdg-foreign handle. The window LibreOffice names for a picker
 can be a hidden one there (window ids mean nothing on Wayland), so the
 active window stands in for it.
Author: Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>
Forwarded: not-needed

